# The scenes of the black-box-tests deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# black-box-tests.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in black-box-tests.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: the lesson's libraries
note "Step 1: the lesson's libraries: a database, a client for its web requests, and a stand-in warehouse."
show lessons/black-box-tests/example/build.gradle.kts "/^dependencies/" "lesson build file" --zoom 10-12

## Scene 2: the application as it ships
note "The order service as it ships: started from a *settings file*."
show OrderService 13 20 "the entry point"
show ShopApplication 21 31 "starting the service" --zoom 22-28

## Scene 3: the code under test
note "The code under test: the code that saves orders today. Two rows in one transaction, and *no commit*."
show TodaysOrderTables 19 27 "today's code that saves orders" --zoom 21-23

## Scene 4: the unit tests
note "The *unit tests*: the order rules, with a stand-in warehouse and a list for a database."
show OrderTakingTest 19 34 "the unit tests" --zoom 21-22

## Scene 5: starting the application
note "The *black-box test* starts WireMock, writes a settings file, and starts the service as it ships."
show OrderServiceTest 38 55 "starting the service for each test" --zoom 44-48 --mark 38

## Scene 6: the black-box test
note "It checks only what comes out: the *answer*, the *warehouse call*, and the *rows written*."
show OrderServiceTest 57 69 "the black-box test" --zoom 59-63 --mark 65-68
show OrderServiceTest 81 94 "reading the rows written" --mark 84-87

## Scene 7: the order is lost
note "Run the tests against today's code:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:black-box-tests:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The answer said 201 Created and the stock was put aside, but no rows were written: the order is lost."

## Scene 8: the fixed code that saves orders
note "The fixed code commits the transaction:"
show OrderTables 19 28 "the fixed code that saves orders" --zoom 24
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:black-box-tests:test"
callout "The answer, the warehouse call and the rows written are all what the shop expects."
